{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":3,"output":660,"cacheRead":54861,"cacheWrite":176,"reasoning":406,"totalTokens":55700,"cost":{"input":6.000000000000001e-7,"output":0.000792,"cacheRead":0.00109722,"cacheWrite":0.000044,"total":0.00193382,"totalFromProvider":true}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"text_end","contentIndex":1,"content":"Implemented first-class double underline support.\n\n### Changes\n- Added `double_underline: Optional[bool]` to `Style.__init__`.\n- Added boolean `Style.double_underline` property.\n- Added style aliases:\n  - `double_underline`\n  - `double-underline`\n  - `du`\n- Preserved double underline through style addition and `Style.combine()` via the existing `underline2` bitmask.\n- Added default style entries and reset handling.\n- Added HTML CSS export:\n  - `text-decoration: underline double`\n- Added SVG CSS export:\n  - `text-decoration: underline double;`\n- Markup now supports examples such as:\n  - `[double_underline]Sample[/]`\n  - `[double-underline red]Alert[/]`\n- ANSI output uses SGR `21`.\n\n### Verification\n- Targeted tests passed: **147 passed**\n  - `tests/test_style.py`\n  - `tests/test_markup.py`\n  - `tests/test_console.py`\n- Manual checks confirmed ANSI, HTML, SVG, aliases, and style composition.\n- Full suite had 12 unrelated existing syntax/color snapshot failures caused by differing Pygments color output; **939 tests passed**."}}
