ed project directory tree\n│   ├── coverage_matrix.md      ← Audit report (from audit_coverage)\n│   ├── knowledge/              ← STRICTLY ALL Knowledge Items (*.ki.md) live HERE!\n│   │   ├── _OVERVIEW.ki.md     ← Project overview stub (MUST NOT be deleted)\n│   │   └── <module>.ki.md      ← Module Knowledge Items\n│   └── decisions/              ← Architectural Decision Records (*.md ADRs)\n├── AGENTS.md                   ← Project instructions for AI agents in harness\n└── CLAUDE.md                   ← Instructions for Claude Code / Anthropic\n```\n\n- **`DIR_INDEX.md`** (`.ki-base/DIR_INDEX.md`) — project directory tree.\n- **`doc_config.json`** (`.ki-base/doc_config.json`) — manifest of tracked artifacts.\n- **`_OVERVIEW.ki.md`** (`.ki-base/knowledge/_OVERVIEW.ki.md`) — start here for high-level architecture.\n- **Harness & Agent Instructions Guide**: see `ki://agent-rules.md` or `ki_instructions(document=\"agent-rules\")` for recommended snippets for `AGENTS.md` and `CLAUDE.md`.\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> 1. NEVER place `*.ki.md` files directly in the root of `.ki-base/`. All Knowledge Items must reside in `.ki-base/knowledge/`.\n> 2. NEVER delete `.ki-base/knowledge/`. The initial `_OVERVIEW.ki.md` (~640 bytes) is a bootstrap stub, not a duplicate. Deleting `knowledge/` breaks audit, scaffolding, and dependency analysis.\n\n## 2. Forced Efficiency (Anti-Hallucinations)\n1. **Mandatory Planning Template**:\n   Before making code changes, your initial plan (Implementation Plan) **MUST** include:\n   - **Affected layers**: [which subsystems are affected]\n   - **Read KIs**: [LIST of files from `.ki-base/knowledge/` which you read for this task]. *If the list is empty — read KIs before writing code!*\n   - **KIs Constraints**: [which approaches are prohibited by current architecture]\n\n2. **Strict Adherence**:\n   - Always read relevant KIs before modifying a module.\n- Use `ki_list()` to view all documented items, `ki_search(query=\"...\")` to find topics, and `ki_read(rel_path=\"...\")` to read documentation.\n   - For read-only analysis tools (`audit_coverage`, `generate_dir_index`, `ki_scaffold_status`, `git_diff_secured`), call `ki_call(tool=\"...\")`.\n   - For state-modifying operations (`git_checkpoint`, `write_know_file`, `edit_know_file`, `ki_scaffold`, `create_adr`), call `ki_mutate(tool=\"...\", args={...})`.\n   - To inspect schemas of available tools, call `ki_tools(name=\"<tool_name>\")`.\n   \n## 3. Workflow-driven Execution\n1. Check `ki://workflows/` resources or MCP Prompts if the user asks for a complex documentation task.\n2. These workflows are your \"operating system\". You **MUST** follow their steps exactly as written.\n"}],"details":{"server":"ki-manager","tool":"ki_instructions"},"isError":false,"durationMs":69,"timestamp":1794169905604},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.encrypted\",\"data\":\"gAAAAABq8NwzGZ1xxwvWZcMex7Yuwd_Qxsz_0h1zt6Ddc5awTP8KVi6OMiih1wB6eevQY4Ir3WjggDzT_VSDynXrHe5NqkYjBb4pT4ZEWmbmOeLgfXi1n_yhcS6tUq-0p2OwrX5FIsqj-8XKR__EGLAJWzAsv5GXULJZvEABmLw0ZVVHCqiHr0re3LkKp4T-EV1orU0fVqD6i6Aa0VTXqe7SqPQlm8b-lbghV6AT6IWQSYbGIXrrEK_70upDHLLHSjQ3__UWYlX5Y5ipP_s-5FtGqz_jrNyng7Ryvg2QG08v0BNXGURFTGQR7YF-kc7CHBndVkDD-ISQ1GiXazX2RirOe8B5VpywsIyGKCgB6EyBQY5pvcNT5zcVH_RerdgGe8TWz75PfGnTVYTrNF3QEhS2dWfyvtbzDKBkv6JSIppnls0OePhcx9X6O1FwnnLnogTbsFVNOSLV_9dNWBdb9fS5TdM_21VZSsU5LupAPuOQK2e1FQ2tV-z0mzdePiScpinhusTcw6BibuM10_CSuZH0C7Ok52cmVacWeFfrOseWCEGmLvNT_lMSA3a9pjoMtYycjJylhDNUEMOdFp3kxcoO852v_Xtr-SsDEp5qxHMjDTm5oFRC3cirAPVpQOgFmtu24QPtcvC3ca2Jwp1N8ZEcasU4HQs1WlRnyS4wFoNc3DZfoCKBRuZiuytp4pb1PWBHUYAtr8hhANU8iZHa4xNxdOhNmwAmYwfZLPmDgXZk238PNheFfwvTaqNRE1UbGKwtc1KdIyHjAW-KgyUG2nkk3oxxPyraxC570M7WTupkLKR2ZHl_V7o6xDTtAPNRB8mwIYiBG6fW1g9Ik2ixB6SUu_R9UdlptNC6aPYXjMoY7FZB9Uc6JIi3mdKRn0Q-rT7Qxs-7SBtMmj-EWDT5yfTNMSXAzK9iEwPCIYb5rWY3Z0uOuMGMtUQyojH53_u_65aibXAXTnG7GB1NxFl_M7opdI10wSFV_69frOcTe4OiDNlH9NdFNRW4Z4LM0ggX0Mf4_wKxHFBqYE8kveoi_KR0yBk_kA6pZ