7209,"totalFromProvider":true}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1794169905616,"responseId":"gen-1794169905-BOEHg2MOxTDUSeM60Fms","rawStopReason":"tool_calls","durationMs":2303,"thinkingLevel":"medium"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_OAyk6aYDbJpxWsIBVzz75WMh","toolName":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# ADR-0003: Style Composition & ANSI Sequences\n\n- **Status:** Accepted\n- **Date:** 2026-11-08\n- **Deciders:** Rich Architectural Maintainers\n\n## Context\n\nStyling in terminals requires combining foreground colors, background colors, links, and various text attributes (bold, italic, underline, reverse, etc.). Rich needs an immutable, high-performance styling algebra that supports cascading inheritance, markup parsing, and export to both ANSI terminals and web formats (HTML/SVG).\n\n## Decision\n\n1. **Immutable Style Class:**  \n   The `Style` object is immutable and hashable with internal caching:\n   - Attributes (bold, underline, double_underline, italic, blink, etc.) use tri-state values (`True`, `False`, `None` where `None` indicates inherit/unset).\n2. **Style Composition Algebra (`+` operator):**  \n   Style addition (`style1 + style2`) cascades attributes from left to right:\n   - Attributes defined in `style2` override attributes in `style1` if set (`is not None`).\n   - Unset attributes (`None`) in `style2` inherit values from `style1`.\n3. **ANSI Sequence Mapping & Exporters:**  \n   Every new style modifier must maintain synchronization across:\n   - Terminal ANSI code generator: open code (e.g. `\\x1b[4:2m` or `\\x1b[21m`) and reset/close code.\n   - Default style definitions (`rich/default_styles.py`).\n   - Markup parser (`rich/markup.py`) to recognize `[modifier]...[/]`.\n   - Exporters (`rich/terminal_theme.py`, `rich/_export_format.py`) for SVG and HTML rendering.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Full consistency between CLI console output, HTML export, and SVG snapshots.\n- Guarantees predictable cascading style resolution across nested tags.\n"}],"details":{"server":"ki-manager","tool":"ki_read"},"isError":false,"durationMs":42,"timestamp":1794169907992},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_szTbbqmuO8qqhk7cWziQb3u2","toolName":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<!-- last_verified: 2026-11-08 -->\n# KI: Rich Core (Segments, Styles & Atomic Primitives)\n\n## Overview\nDefines the atomic rendering primitives of Rich: `Segment` (minimal text+style tuple), `Style` (ANSI attributes container), `Rule` (horizontal dividing lines), `Status` (loading indicators with spinners), and alternate screen buffer controls (`Screen`).\n\n## Entry Points & Public API\n- `Style`: Immutable representation of text styling (color, bgcolor, bold, underline, italic, hyperlinks).\n- `Segment`: Lowest-level atomic rendering token yielded by all renderables.\n- `Rule`: Horizontal decorative line with optional centered title.\n- `Status`: Context manager displaying a transient spinner alongside status text during long tasks.\n- `auto`: Decorator automatically generating `__repr__` methods from `__rich_repr__`.\n\n## Key Components\n| Class / Function | File | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|\n| `Segment` | `rich/segment.py` | Atomic renderable unit containing text string, Style instance, and optional control codes |\n| `Style` | `rich/style.py` | High-level style definitions supporting color blending, negation, and OSC 8 hyperlinks |\n| `Rule` | `rich/rule.py` | Horizontal separator line with custom box character and title alignment |\n| `Status` | `rich/status.py` | Transient loading animation utilizing `Spinner` and live console display |\n| `Spinner` | `rich/spinner.py` | Animated ASCII/Unicode spinner renderable advancing frame by frame |\n| `Screen` | `rich/screen.py` | Fullscreen terminal display switcher toggling alternate screen buffers |\n| `auto` | `rich/repr.py` | Class decorator generating `__repr__` from `__rich_repr__` |\n| `render_scope` | `rich/scope.py` | Renders a table of local/global variables with syntax styling |\n\n## Testing & Verification\n- Test commands: `pytest tests/test_segment.py tests/test_style.py tests/test_rule.py tests/test_spinner.py tests/test_status.py`\n- Test files: `tests/test_segment.py`, `tests/test_style.py`, `tests/test_rule.py`, `tests/test_spinner.py`, `tests/test_status.py`\n\n## Non-obvious Details\n- **Segment splitting and line breaking**: `Segment.split_and_crop_lines` partitions segment streams into line arrays strictly respecting character cell widths and ANSI boundaries.\n- **Style Bitmask & Attributes in `rich/style.py` (ADR-0003)**:\n  - `STYLE_ATTRIBUTES` (L106–L126): Maps style names and short aliases (`\"b\"`, `\"u\"`, `\"uu\"`, `\"underline2\"`, `\"double_underline\"`, `\"double-underline\"`, `\"du\"`) to internal attribute names (`\"underline2\"` uses `_Bit(9)` / bitmask value 512 at L171, L189, L284).\n  - `Style.__init__` (L131–L195): Accepts boolean flags (`underline`, `underline2`, `double_underline`). If `double_underline is not None: underline2 = double_underline`. Expose `@property def double_underline(self) -> bool: return bool(self.underline2)` around L290.\n  - `Style.get_html_style` (L564–L605): Builds CSS rules for HTML export. At L589–L596, check `if self.underline2: append(\"text-decoration: underline double\")` before `elif self.underline: append(\"text-decoration: underline\")`.\n  - Default style catalog in `rich/default_styles.py` (L20–L35): Maps `\"underline\"`, `\"double_underline\"`, `\"double-underline\"` to `Style(...)` instances so markup tags like `[double_underline]...[/]` resolve automatically.\n- **Style arithmetic**: Styles can be combined using addition (`style1 + style2`), where the right-hand operand overrides attributes defined in the left-hand operand via `_attributes` and `_set_attributes` bitmasks.\n- **Hyperlink support**: `Style(link=\"https://...\")` embeds standard OSC 8 terminal hyperlinks that modern terminal emulators make clickable.\n\n## Common Pitfalls\n- **Segment mutation**: `Segment` instances should be treated as immutable. Modifying the `.text` of a segment directly breaks cell width caches.\n- **Status nesting**: Attempting to run multiple nested `Status` spinners on the same console without distinct Live contexts causes display corruption.\n\n\n## Related KIs\n- [[KI_rich_align.md]] (via `rich/align.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_align.md]] (via `rich/cells.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_align.md]] (via `rich/console.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_default.md]] (via `rich/highlighter.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_default.md]] (via `rich/jupyter.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_emoji.md]] (via `rich/__init__.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_emoji.md]] (via `rich/color.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_live.md]] (via `rich/_loop.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_live.md]] (via `rich/live.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_markdown.md]] (via `rich/measure.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_markdown.md]] (via `rich/panel.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_markdown.md]] (via `rich/pretty.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_null.md]] (via `rich/_spinners.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_syntax.md]] (via `rich/syntax.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_syntax.md]] (via `rich/table.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_syntax.md]] (via `rich/terminal_theme.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_syntax.md]] (via `rich/text.py`)\n\n"}],"details":{"server":"ki-manager","tool":"ki_read"},"isError":false,"durationMs":50,"timestamp":1794169907995},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_SKa69ss6C54uT1XXps5jwuAS","toolName":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<!-- last_verified: 2026-11-08 -->\n# KI: Rich Core (Console, Alignment & Core Layouts)\n\n## Overview\nCentral pipeline of Rich: houses the primary `Console` class, ANSI escape sequence decoder, cell width calculators, border box constants, and alignment/column containers. It coordinates measurement, rendering, and terminal stream emission.\n\n## Entry Points & Public API\n- `Console`: Primary interface orchestrating rendering, style resolution, capture buffers, and terminal IO.\n- `Align`: Alignment wrapper centering or aligning child renderables horizontally and vertically.\n- `Columns`: Flow container rendering items into flowing horizontal columns.\n- `Box`: Border character definitions (e.g. `ROUNDED`, `SQUARE`, `DOUBLE`).\n- `AnsiDecoder`: State machine converting raw ANSI escape strings into styled `Text` objects.\n\n## Key Components\n| Class / Function | File | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|\n| `Console` | `rich/console.py` | Central rendering engine managing color depth, terminal capabilities, output streams, and paging |\n| `Align` | `rich/align.py` | Alignment container placing renderables left, center, or right with optional padding |\n| `AnsiDecoder` | `rich/ansi.py` | State machine parsing ANSI escape codes into Rich segments |\n| `Box` | `rich/box.py` | Border character sets for panels, tables, and frames |\n| `cell_len` / `set_cell_size` | `rich/cells.py` | Character cell width measurement accounting for double-width CJK and zero-width characters |\n| `Columns` | `rich/columns.py` | Renders a collection of items into responsive terminal columns |\n| `Constrain` | `rich/constrain.py` | Limits child renderable width to a specified maximum bound |\n| `Control` | `rich/control.py` | Emits raw terminal control sequences (cursor position, title changes, screen clears) |\n\n## Testing & Verification\n- Test commands: `pytest tests/test_console.py tests/test_align.py tests/test_ansi.py tests/test_box.py tests/test_columns.py`\n- Test files: `tests/test_console.py`, `tests/test_align.py`, `tests/test_ansi.py`, `tests/test_box.py`, `tests/test_columns.py`\n\n## Non-obvious Details\n- **Automatic stream sniffing**: `Console` checks `COLORTERM`, `TERM`, `FORCE_COLOR`, and `NO_COLOR` upon initialization. If stdout is redirected to a pipe or file, color highlighting is stripped unless `force_terminal=True`.\n- **Double-width character calculation**: `cell_len()` does not use string `len()`; it queries character codepoint tables in `_unicode_data` to properly account for wide East Asian symbols and multi-byte emojis.\n- **Recording & SVG/HTML Export (`rich/console.py`, L2260–L2420)**: `Console(record=True)` stores all rendered segments into an internal buffer, exportable via `export_text()`, `export_html()`, or `export_svg()`. In `Console.export_svg` (L2342–L2415), the internal `get_svg_style(style: Style)` helper at L2390–L2405 constructs `css_rules` for each segment (`if style.underline2: css_rules.append(\"text-decoration: underline double;\") elif style.underline: css_rules.append(\"text-decoration: underline;\")`).\n\n## Common Pitfalls\n- **Mismatched width constraints**: Wrapping a wide table or syntax block inside `Align.center` with `width` exceeding terminal dimensions will cause line wraps that ruin horizontal centering.\n- **Paging blocking**: Using `Console.pager()` captures the terminal interactively; running it inside automated or headless test runners will hang waiting for user keypresses.\n\n\n## Related KIs\n- [[KI_rich_default.md]] (via `rich/highlighter.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_default.md]] (via `rich/json.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_default.md]] (via `rich/jupyter.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_emoji.md]] (via `rich/_emoji_replace.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_emoji.md]] (via `rich/_unicode_data/__init__.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_emoji.md]] (via `rich/_windows.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_emoji.md]] (via `rich/_windows_renderer.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_emoji.md]] (via `rich/color.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_emoji.md]] (via `rich/emoji.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_live.md]] (via `rich/_export_format.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_live.md]] (via `rich/_fileno.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_live.md]] (via `rich/_log_render.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_live.md]] (via `rich/_loop.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_live.md]] (via `rich/live.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_markdown.md]] (via `rich/markup.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_markdown.md]] (via `rich/measure.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_markdown.md]] (via `rich/padding.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_markdown.md]] (via `rich/pager.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_markdown.md]] (via `rich/panel.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_markdown.md]] (via `rich/pretty.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_markdown.md]] (via `rich/protocol.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_null.md]] (via `rich/_null_file.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_null.md]] (via `rich/_win32_console.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_region.md]] (via `rich/region.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_region.md]] (via `rich/rule.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_region.md]] (via `rich/scope.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_region.md]] (via `rich/screen.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_region.md]] (via `rich/segment.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_region.md]] (via `rich/status.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_region.md]] (via `rich/style.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_region.md]] (via `rich/styled.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_syntax.md]] (via `rich/table.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_syntax.md]] (via `rich/terminal_theme.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_syntax.md]] (via `rich/text.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_syntax.md]] (via `rich/theme.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_syntax.md]] (via `rich/traceback.py`)\n\n"}],"details":{"server":"ki-manager","tool":"ki_read"},"isError":false,"durationMs":65,"timestamp":1794169908003},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_6nzPhnqCvcQ7k3NSVGkOove1","toolName":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<!-- last_verified: 2026-11-08 -->\n# KI: Rich Core (Markdown, Markup, Panels & Prompts)\n\n## Overview\nProvides markdown document parsing, console markup parsing (`[bold red]...[/]`), framed panel containers (`Panel`), recursive object pretty-printing (`Pretty`), user interactive prompts (`Prompt`), and the Rich Console Protocol definitions.\n\n## Entry Points & Public API\n- `Markdown`: Renderable converting CommonMark Markdown specifications into stylized terminal blocks.\n- `Panel`: Framed container with border styles, title, and subtitle around any renderable.\n- `Pretty`: Recursive data structure pretty-printer handling cyclic references and custom indentation.\n- `Prompt` / `Confirm`: Interactive CLI input prompts with validation, default values, and type coercion.\n- `escape`: Utility escaping square bracket markup tags in arbitrary text.\n\n## Key Components\n| Class / Function | File | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|\n| `Markdown` | `rich/markdown.py` | AST walker converting markdown elements (headings, code blocks, lists, blockquotes) into renderables |\n| `render` / `escape` | `rich/markup.py` | Parser converting `[tag]text[/tag]` markup strings into styled `Text` spans |\n| `Panel` | `rich/panel.py` | Boxed border container enclosing renderables with titles and alignment |\n| `Pretty` | `rich/pretty.py` | Data structure formatter handling dicts, dataclasses, pydantic models, and recursion |\n| `Prompt` / `Confirm` | `rich/prompt.py` | Interactive console prompt asking questions and verifying user answers |\n| `Measurement` | `rich/measure.py` | Minimum and maximum width calculation protocol (`__rich_measure__`) |\n| `Padding` | `rich/padding.py` | Surrounds a renderable with top, right, bottom, and left whitespace margins |\n| `is_renderable` | `rich/protocol.py` | Introspection helper checking if an object implements Rich protocols |\n\n## Testing & Verification\n- Test commands: `pytest tests/test_markdown.py tests/test_markup.py tests/test_panel.py tests/test_pretty.py tests/test_prompt.py`\n- Test files: `tests/test_markdown.py`, `tests/test_markup.py`, `tests/test_panel.py`, `tests/test_pretty.py`, `tests/test_prompt.py`\n\n## Non-obvious Details\n- **The Rich Console Protocol**: An object is renderable if it defines `__rich__() -> Renderable` or generator `__rich_console__(console, options) -> Iterable[RenderResult]`.\n- **Measurement negotiation**: Containers query children using `Measurement.get(console, options, renderable)` before layout allocation to determine optimal width.\n- **Markup tag stack**: `markup.py` maintains an internal tag stack. Self-closing tags or single closing slashes (`[/]`) pop the most recent active style off the stack.\n\n## Common Pitfalls\n- **Unclosed markup tags**: Forgetting to close tags like `[bold]` can lead to unexpected syntax errors (`MarkupError`) if strict parsing is enabled.\n- **Prompt stdin EOF**: Calling `Prompt.ask()` in non-interactive CI environments without mocked stdin results in an unhandled `EOFError`.\n\n\n## Related KIs\n- [[KI_rich_align.md]] (via `rich/align.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_align.md]] (via `rich/box.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_align.md]] (via `rich/cells.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_align.md]] (via `rich/console.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_align.md]] (via `rich/containers.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_default.md]] (via `rich/errors.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_default.md]] (via `rich/highlighter.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_default.md]] (via `rich/jupyter.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_emoji.md]] (via `rich/__init__.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_emoji.md]] (via `rich/_emoji_replace.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_emoji.md]] (via `rich/color.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_emoji.md]] (via `rich/color_triplet.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_emoji.md]] (via `rich/emoji.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_live.md]] (via `rich/_loop.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_null.md]] (via `rich/_pick.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_null.md]] (via `rich/_stack.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_null.md]] (via `rich/abc.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_region.md]] (via `rich/repr.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_region.md]] (via `rich/rule.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_region.md]] (via `rich/segment.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_region.md]] (via `rich/style.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_syntax.md]] (via `rich/syntax.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_syntax.md]] (via `rich/table.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_syntax.md]] (via `rich/text.py`)\n\n"}],"details":{"server":"ki-manager","tool":"ki_read"},"isError":false,"durationMs":58,"timestamp":1794169908011},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Inspecting targeted files**\n\nI need to take a closer look at the actual files that grep is targeting. It seems important to confirm those details. I want to ensure I'm understanding exactly what I'm working with so I can analyze them properly. There might be specific patterns or elements I should pay attention to within those files. Let's make sure to check them thoroughly to capture all relevant information!","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.summary\",\"summary\":\"**Inspecting targeted files**\\n\\nI need to take a closer look at the actual files that grep is targeting. It seems important to confirm those details. I want to ensure I'm understanding exactly wha